      },
      "text": "Mayr (1942): reproductive isolation is the criterion. All major species concepts,\ntheir failure domains, and the formal property each captures:"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SPECIATION.md#008",
      "path": [
        "04-SPECIATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation, git-history:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "concepts": "[speciation]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:speciation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[speciation]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Speciation: Mechanisms and Models",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Concept | Criterion | Fails for | What it captures |\n|---------|-----------|-----------|-----------------|\n| Biological (BSC) | Reproductive isolation | Asexuals, bacteria, allopatric pops, ring species | Gene flow barrier |\n| Phylogenetic (PSC) | Smallest diagnosable clade | Over-splits (many more \"species\" than BSC) | Genealogical exclusivity |\n| Ecological | Distinct adaptive zone | Hard to define zone objectively | Niche occupation |\n| Cohesion | Genetic + ecological exchangeability | Complex to operationalize | Both forces of cohesion |\n| Genotypic cluster | Statistical gap in genotype space | Arbitrary threshold | Empirical data-driven |"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SPECIATION.md#009",
      "path": [
        "04-SPECIATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation, git-history:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "concepts": "[speciation]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:speciation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
