        "root_concepts": "[speciation]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Speciation: Mechanisms and Models",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "\"Species\" is a human category on a continuum. The 26 competing concepts reflect\nthat speciation is a process, not a discrete transition."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SPECIATION.md#010",
      "path": [
        "04-SPECIATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation, git-history:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "concepts": "[speciation]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:speciation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[speciation]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Speciation: Mechanisms and Models",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Formal framing**: reproductive isolation RI ∈ [0,1]. Total RI = 1 − ∏(1 − RIᵢ)\nwhere each barrier i contributes a partial isolation value. Two populations can be\n70% reproductively isolated with no principled threshold where they \"become species.\""
    },
