      "text": "## Allopatric Speciation"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SPECIATION.md#013",
      "path": [
        "04-SPECIATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation, git-history:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "concepts": "[speciation]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:speciation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[speciation]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Speciation: Mechanisms and Models",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The dominant mode. Geographic barrier prevents gene flow; populations diverge\nindependently; secondary contact tests whether reproductive isolation has evolved."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SPECIATION.md#014",
      "path": [
        "04-SPECIATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation, git-history:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation]",
        "canonical_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "concepts": "[speciation]",
        "current_path": "evolutionary-biology/04-SPECIATION.md",
        "id": "maxim:evolutionary-biology:speciation",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "evolutionary-biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[speciation]",
        "section": "evolutionary-biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Speciation: Mechanisms and Models",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  PROCESS:\n  ─────────\n  1. Ancestral population occupies continuous range\n  2. Vicariance event: geographic barrier splits population\n     (mountain uplift, sea level rise, continental drift, habitat change)\n  3. Allopatric populations evolve independently\n     - Genetic drift accumulates differences\n     - Local adaptation drives divergence\n     - Dobzhansky-Muller incompatibilities develop\n  4. Secondary contact:\n     - If RI complete: species coexist, character displacement\n     - If RI partial: hybridization, hybrid zone\n     - If RI minimal: populations merge (reticulation)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SPECIATION.md#015",
      "path": [
        "04-SPECIATION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation, git-history:evolutionary-biology:04-speciation]",
